		<title>Anthropic&#039;s Claude Fable 5.2 doesn&#039;t generate images, it paints them</title>
		<link>https://the-decoder.com/anthropics-claude-fable-5-2-doesnt-generate-images-it-paints-them/</link>
					<comments>https://the-decoder.com/anthropics-claude-fable-5-2-doesnt-generate-images-it-paints-them/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Manuel Uth]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:42:03 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[AI in practice]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Artificial Intelligence]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Anthropic]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Claude]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Fable 5.2]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://the-decoder.com/?p=42896</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p><img width="1376" height="768" src="https://the-decoder.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/claude_fable_5.2_painting.png" class="attachment-full size-full wp-post-image" alt="" style="height: auto; margin-bottom: 10px;" decoding="async" /></p>
<p>        Anthropic's Claude Fable 5.2 doesn't generate images the way other AI models do. Instead of computing pixels, the language model writes Python code that places hundreds of thousands of simulated brushstrokes on a virtual canvas, complete with bristle texture and paint application. A single photorealistic parking garage scene took roughly 700,000 strokes, according to Anthropic employee Jake Eaton.</p>
<p>The article <a href="https://the-decoder.com/anthropics-claude-fable-5-2-doesnt-generate-images-it-paints-them/">Anthropic&#039;s Claude Fable 5.2 doesn&#039;t generate images, it paints them</a> appeared first on <a href="https://the-decoder.com">The Decoder</a>.</p>
]]></description>
		
